  "details": "I had been suffering from persistent crashes when launching VRChat in any mode on PC. None of the guides proposed methods fixed this for me. Including whitelisting EAC, SteamVR and VRChat in both Firewalls and AV's, disabling my AV and a hundred more proposed fixes.\n\n1. Having both Mullvad VPN and Bitdefender installed\n\n2. Launch VRChat\n\n3. Crash :(\n\nI deleted my EAC sys file and uninstalled both Bitdefender and Mullvad, now VRChat works flawlessly. I can't pinpoint what specifically is the cause but I'd lean towards Bitdefender having some sort of conflict with EAC or Unity. Notably, this problem is reproduceable on the game 'Squad' which also uses EAC.",
